# Uptime Kuma Docker Environment Variables

# Web UI Port
UPTIME_KUMA_PORT=3001

# Docker Socket
# =============
# The Docker socket is mounted read-only to enable container health monitoring.
# This allows Uptime Kuma to monitor internal container health status rather
# than just pinging exposed ports.
#
# To disable Docker integration, remove the socket volume mount.

# First Run
# =========
# On first access, you'll be prompted to create an admin account.
# No default credentials exist.
